---
import { rich } from '../lib/rich.mjs';
import { bars, clusters, lines } from '../lib/viz.mjs';
import triton from '../data/triton.json';

const r = rich;
const GH = 'https://github.com/';
const RESUME = '/Harshith_Kantamneni_GPU_Kernel_Resume.pdf';

// #1319: this PR over the authors' kernels, 8 shapes on H100
const ratio = [
  ['B=8, T=1024, H=16, D=128', 1.04], ['B=4, T=2048, H=16, D=128', 1.07], ['B=2, T=4096, H=16, D=128', 1.16], ['B=1, T=8192, H=16, D=128', 1.20],
  ['B=4, T=2048, H=32, D=64', 1.42], ['Packed 512+2048+512+5120, H=16, D=128', 1.07], ['Packed 8×1024, H=32, D=64', 1.32], ['Packed 8192, H=16, D=128', 1.19],
];
// #1412: one decode step against recomputing the prefix, H200, microseconds, both axes log
const keys = ['T=1024', 'T=4096', 'T=16384', 'T=65536'];
const speedup = ['1.0×', '3.4×', '13.1×', '52.7×'];
const decode = [72.4, 275.0, 1082.4, 4301.8];
const recompute = [72.8, 929.4, 14190.3, 226529.2];
const xs = [7, 35.67, 64.33, 93];
const logY = (v) => (1 - (Math.log10(v) - 1.3) / (5.7 - 1.3)) * 100;
// #1223: at batch 1
const gqa = [['64/8 d128', 14.57, 6.66, 3.30, '2.19×'], ['64/8 d64', 8.23, 4.23, 4.09, '1.95×'], ['32/8 d128', 9.91, 6.66, 3.30, '1.49×'], ['32/2 d256', 17.15, 12.55, 9.96, '1.37×'], ['8/1 d128', 7.59, 6.63, 3.30, '1.15×']];
// Default head mapping shown without scripts
const q0 = 8, kv0 = 4;
const heads = (fn) => Array.from({ length: q0 }, (_, h) => fn(h));
const good = heads((h) => Math.floor(h / (q0 / kv0)));
const bad = heads((h) => Math.floor(h / kv0) % kv0);
const cell = (x) => `<i class="c${x % 4}" data-n="${x}"></i>`;

// Triton scatter from the raw benchmark file
const W = 640, H = 380, L = 44, T = 14, Rr = 12, B = 44;
const ms = [...new Set(triton.map((p) => p.M))].sort((a, b) => a - b);
const yMin = 0.5, yMax = 1.8;
const y = (v) => T + (1 - (v - yMin) / (yMax - yMin)) * (H - T - B);
const groups = ms.map((m) => triton.filter((p) => p.M === m));
const xBand = (W - L - Rr) / ms.length;
const xOf = (p) => { const i = ms.indexOf(p.M), g = groups[i], k = g.indexOf(p); return L + xBand * i + xBand * ((k + 1) / (g.length + 1)); };
const best = (key) => triton.reduce((m, p) => (p[key] > m[key] ? p : m));
const dots = (key) => triton.map((p) => {
  const v = p[key];
  return `<circle class="${v > 1 ? 'up' : ''}" cx="${xOf(p).toFixed(1)}" cy="${y(v).toFixed(1)}" r="${v > 1 ? 5 : 4}" data-s="M=${p.M}, N=${p.N}, K=${p.K}" data-v="${v.toFixed(2)}"></circle>`;
}).join('');
---
<section class="opener bright" id="kernels" data-chapter="k" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Kernels</h2>
    <p set:html={r('Where the time actually goes. [[count.merged|3 PRs merged]]: Triton attention kernels and KV-cache decoding in flash-linear-attention, and tests in NVIDIA cuDNN frontend.')} />
    <div class="ol">
      <a href="#merged">The merged kernels</a>
      <a href="#gqa">The copy and the tests</a>
      <a href="#blind">The timing model</a>
      <a href="#triton">Fusing kernels</a>
      <a href="/kernels/">Only the kernel work</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="k" data-chapter="k" data-resume={RESUME}>
  <section class="scene" id="merged" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">Kernels that merged, and where they still lag</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame" data-f="0">
              <figcaption>Shared memory per kernel, H100</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[pr1319.tiles|57-89 KiB]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">with 64×32 tiles, where 64×64 tiles needed 129-193 KiB</p>
              <div class="big">
                <Fragment set:html={bars([
                  { label: '64×64 tiles', value: 193, text: '129-193 KiB', tone: 'dim' },
                  { label: '64×32 tiles', value: 89, text: '57-89 KiB' },
                ], { max: 193 })} />
              </div>
            </figure>
            <figure class="frame" data-f="1">
              <figcaption>This PR's time over the original authors', forward plus backward, H100</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[pr1319.vs_authors|1.04-1.42×]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">the authors' time, slower on all 8 shapes. The left edge is parity.</p>
              <div class="sm">
                <Fragment set:html={bars(ratio.map(([label, v]) => ({ label, value: v, text: v.toFixed(2) + '×' })), { min: 1, max: 1.5 })} />
              </div>
            </figure>
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="2">
              <figcaption>One decode step against recomputing the prefix, H200, batch 1, microseconds, log scale</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[sbk.op|52.7×]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">faster than recomputing at 64K keys, with no gain at 1024</p>
              <div class="legend"><span><i></i>Decode with the cache</span><span><i class="mid"></i>Recompute the prefix</span></div>
              <Fragment set:html={lines({
                xs, y: logY, height: 230,
                series: [
                  { values: recompute, color: 'var(--mid)', side: 'above', labels: recompute.map((v) => v.toFixed(1)) },
                  { values: decode, color: 'var(--k)', side: 'below', labels: decode.map((v) => v.toFixed(1)) },
                ],
              })} />
              <div class="lc-x">
                {keys.map((k, i) => <span style={`left:${xs[i]}%`} class={i === 0 ? 'start' : i === keys.length - 1 ? 'end' : ''}>{k}<b>{speedup[i]}</b></span>)}
              </div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p>Forward and backward Triton kernels for stick-breaking attention, merged into flash-linear-attention after review caught a silent zero gradient. Smaller tiles cut shared memory by about half.</p></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('They\'re still slower than the original authors\' kernels. Nsight Compute shows no saturated pipe at [[pr1319.occupancy|about 12% occupancy]], so I read the gap as stalls on fp32 scans.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p set:html={r('#1412 added KV-cache decoding. The speedup grows with keys, but at model level a token still takes [[sbk.model|about 9 ms]], and I haven\'t profiled why.')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href="/work/stick-breaking-kernels/">Read the case study</a>
            <a href={GH + 'fla-org/flash-linear-attention/pull/1319'}>#1319</a>
            <a href={GH + 'fla-org/flash-linear-attention/pull/1412'}>#1412</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="gqa" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">The copy took longer than the math</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame" data-f="0">
              <figcaption>One attention call in NVIDIA cuDNN, A100, 64 query heads and 8 KV heads, 128K cache</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[pr1223.copy|7.28 ms]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">copying K and V, before attention began</p>
              <div class="big">
                <Fragment set:html={bars([
                  { label: 'K/V copies', value: 7.28, text: '7.28 ms' },
                  { label: 'Attention', value: 6.7, text: '6.0-6.7 ms', tone: 'dim' },
                ], { max: 8 })} />
              </div>
            </figure>
            <figure class="frame" data-f="1">
              <figcaption>Multi-token steps at batch 1, A100, milliseconds. Query heads/KV heads, head dimension.</figcaption>
              <p class="f-read" set:html={r('[[pr1223.kv|1.15-2.19×]]')} />
              <p class="f-sub">faster with the copies gone, and the backend stayed faster still</p>
              <div class="legend"><span><i class="dim"></i>Develop</span><span><i></i>My prototype</span><span><i class="mid"></i>cuDNN backend</span></div>
              <Fragment set:html={clusters(gqa.map(([label, dv, pr, be, x]) => ({
                label, note: x,
                bars: [
                  { value: dv, text: dv.toFixed(2), tone: 'dim' },
                  { value: pr, text: pr.toFixed(2) },
                  { value: be, text: be.toFixed(2), tone: 'mid' },
                ],
              })), { max: 18 })} />
            </figure>
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="2">
              <figcaption>Which KV head does each query head read? Pick a shape.</figcaption>
              <div class="seg" id="heads" role="group" aria-label="Query heads over KV heads" style="margin-top:10px">
                <button type="button" data-q="4" data-kv="2" aria-pressed="false">4/2</button>
                <button type="button" data-q="16" data-kv="4" aria-pressed="false">16/4</button>
                <button type="button" data-q="8" data-kv="4" aria-pressed="true">8/4</button>
                <button type="button" data-q="8" data-kv="2" aria-pressed="false">8/2</button>
              </div>
              <p class="f-h">Correct formula</p>
              <div class="cells" id="hm-a" style={`grid-template-columns:repeat(${q0},minmax(0,1fr))`} aria-label={`Correct mapping: ${good.join(' ')}`} role="img" set:html={good.map(cell).join('')} />
              <p class="f-h">The bug NVIDIA's tests missed</p>
              <div class="cells" id="hm-b" style={`grid-template-columns:repeat(${q0},minmax(0,1fr))`} aria-label={`Buggy mapping: ${bad.join(' ')}`} role="img" set:html={bad.map(cell).join('')} />
              <p class="verdict" id="hm-v" role="status">Different mapping. A test at this shape catches the bug.</p>
              <p class="f-note" set:html={r('With bugs planted, NVIDIA\'s SM80 suite still reported [[gqa.planted|All 411 pass]]. My tests caught all [[pr1287.bugs|3 injected bugs]].')} />
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p>At one shape on an A100, NVIDIA's cuDNN path spent longer copying K and V than running attention. It writes the same data out once per query head.</p></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('I removed the copies in a prototype. [[pr1223.batched|6 batched rows 2.6-3.3×]] faster, and [[pr1223.oom|10 more]] stopped running out of memory. The backend stayed faster on [[pr1223.backend|27 of 31]] multi-token rows.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p>NVIDIA then shipped native GQA in #1239, so I closed mine and merged tests instead. Their tests used 4/2 and 16/4 heads, where the wrong formula gives the right answer. Try it.</p></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href="/work/cudnn-gqa/">Read the case study</a>
            <a href="/notes/kv-copies-gqa/">The worklog</a>
            <a href={GH + 'NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend/pull/1287'}>#1287</a>
            <a href={GH + 'NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend/pull/1223'}>#1223</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="blind" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">Predict the kernel before running it</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1,2">
              <figcaption>Prediction error, rms, one GH200. Lower is better. The tick is the bar each test had to clear.</figcaption>
              <div class="from1">
                <p class="grp">Model v3, one test tile, time predictions</p>
                <Fragment set:html={bars([
                  { label: 'Mixtral-8x7B', value: 0.51, text: '0.51%' }, { label: 'Phi-3.5-MoE', value: 0.69, text: '0.69%' }, { label: 'OLMoE', value: 0.54, text: '0.54%' },
                ], { max: 20, mark: 2 })} />
              </div>
              <div class="from2">
                <p class="grp">Decode model, on models it hadn't seen in decode</p>
                <Fragment set:html={bars([
                  { label: 'DeepSeek-V2-Lite', value: 2.35, text: '2.35%', tone: 'dim' }, { label: 'Qwen1.5', value: 5.3, text: '5.3%', tone: 'dim' }, { label: 'Phi-3.5', value: 9.5, text: '9.5%', tone: 'dim' },
                  { label: 'Granite-3B', value: 13.4, text: '13.4%', tone: 'dim' }, { label: 'JetMoE', value: 19.5, text: '19.5%', tone: 'dim' },
                ], { max: 20, mark: 1.5 })} />
              </div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p>I built a timing model of vLLM's fused MoE kernel: give it the routing and the tile, and it predicts each call's time. I froze its predictions before renting the GPU, so results couldn't tune them.</p></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('On one [[mk.v3|32×64×64]] test tile, model v3\'s time predictions held at [[mk.v3|0.51-0.69%]] rms. Its byte predictions missed by [[mk.v3|11.76%]] on OLMoE\'s first wave.')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p set:html={r('The decode blind test failed: [[mk.decode|11.4%]] rms pooled, against a [[mk.decode|1.5%]] bar. No model is blind-certified on vLLM\'s own tiles yet.')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href={GH + 'harshithkantamneni/moe-kernels/tree/gh200-analysis-2026-09-27'}>The public repo</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene" id="triton" data-scene>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h3 class="scene-t">Fusing kernels wasn't automatically faster</h3>
      <div class="scene-g">
        <div class="stage">
          <div class="frames">
            <figure class="frame key" data-f="0,1,2">
              <figcaption>Fused Triton kernel against the unfused path, 76 shapes on an A100. Hover a dot for its shape.</figcaption>
              <div class="seg" id="scatter-seg" role="group" aria-label="Precision" style="margin-top:10px">
                <button type="button" data-v="fp16" aria-pressed="true">fp16</button>
                <button type="button" data-v="bf16" aria-pressed="false">bf16</button>
              </div>
              <div class="plot" id="scatter" tabindex="0">
                <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Speedup of each shape against the unfused path. In fp16 the median is 0.96 times, 27 of 76 shapes are faster and the best is 1.73 times.">
                  <line x1={L} x2={W - Rr} y1={y(1)} y2={y(1)} stroke="var(--quiet)" stroke-dasharray="4 4"></line>
                  {[1.6, 1.4, 1.2, 1, 0.8, 0.6].map((v) => <text x={L - 8} y={y(v) + 4} text-anchor="end">{v}×</text>)}
                  {ms.map((m, i) => <text x={L + xBand * (i + 0.5)} y={H - 22} text-anchor="middle">{m}</text>)}
                  <text x={L + (W - L - Rr) / 2} y={H - 4} text-anchor="middle">Rows in the GEMM (M)</text>
                  <g data-g="fp16"><Fragment set:html={dots('fp16')} /><text class="from1 best" x={xOf(best('fp16')) + 10} y={y(best('fp16').fp16) + 5}>{best('fp16').fp16.toFixed(2)}×</text></g>
                  <g data-g="bf16"><Fragment set:html={dots('bf16')} /><text class="from1 best" x={xOf(best('bf16')) + 10} y={y(best('bf16').bf16) + 5}>{best('bf16').bf16.toFixed(2)}×</text></g>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <p class="f-note">Dots above the dashed line are faster than the unfused path.</p>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step" data-step="0"><p set:html={r('Eager PyTorch runs a projection as separate kernels: a GEMM, then bias, then GeLU. I built one Triton kernel that does all three and benchmarked [[tri.shapes|76 LLM-shaped GEMMs]].')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="1"><p set:html={r('One shape ran [[tri.best|1.73×]] faster than the unfused path. Across all of them: [[tri.median|Median 0.96×]], and only [[tri.faster|27 faster]].')} /></div>
          <div class="step" data-step="2"><p set:html={r('I first read this as small batches being memory-bound. The counts don\'t support that: fused is faster on [[tri.ridge|10 of 30]] cells left of the ridge and [[tri.ridge|42 of 122]] right of it. So I corrected it.')} /></div>
          <div class="scene-links">
            <a href={GH + 'harshithkantamneni/triton-vs-cublas-llm-benchmarks'}>Code and raw data</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scene also">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="alsos">
        <div>
          <h4><a href={GH + 'NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3591'}>TransformerEngine #3591</a></h4>
          <p>CUDA kernel for grouped NVFP4 dequantization, reading offsets on device. Output matches per-tensor results bitwise. I haven't timed it.</p>
          <p class="st">Open, in review</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4><a href={GH + 'vllm-project/vllm/pull/38338'}>vLLM #38338</a></h4>
          <p set:html={r('Triton NVFP4 GEMM reference holding [[pr38338.tflops|1,014-1,076 TFLOP/s]] on RTX 5090 for one shape. Weakest shape: [[pr38338.weak|0.53-0.57×]] CUTLASS.')} />
          <p class="st">Closed, not merged</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
